Z||000000||Htown86GT||03-28-2001||03:10 PM||||Last nights thunderstorms in houston somehow zapped my fiero, when i woke up this morning i could hear the dying warbles of my alarm.  Now the car's fuel pump wont stop, I had to take the fuse for the fuel pump out to get it to stop.  Any idea what would cause this problem??<P>------------------<BR>WHat The Heck is That?!  Oh Just my 86' GT <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.rav-ee.com/images/Myfiero.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||DaveL||03-28-2001||04:38 PM||||Sounds like a lightning strike in the near vicinity of your vehicle, thereby generating an electromagnetic pulse which confused your cars electronics...either that or your girlfriend plugged her hairdryer into the cigarette lighter and left it running...<BR>Seriously, never heard of anything like that. I'd suspect it was haunted!<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Htown86GT||03-28-2001||05:00 PM||||hehe........ Interesting theory, to bad you werent on the team investigating the Kennedy assination!<P>Ohhh well... hmm.||||reg||14
Z||000003||Formula88||03-28-2001||05:03 PM||||I've heard of it.  Happened to me once.  You car either got hit by lightening, or more likely, lightening struck very close by.  The EMP has somehow fried your electronics.  Check to see if any fuses are blown.  Chances are, you're ECM may be damaged.  When it happened to me, I was driving in my GN and my friend was in his Motley Carlo SS right beside me.  As we passed under a power line on the expressway, lightening struck the power line.  My car was unaffected (except for all the wax on my roof being melted off!) but Steve's SS started running like crap.  Turned out his ECM was fried.  He had been playing with the PROM chip earlier and hadn't put all the covers back on the ECM and thus, it didn't have any shielding that it would normally have.  I guess I was just lucky, or you got a heavier EMP than I did.  Still, the look of that big round spot of no wax on the roof of my car was eerie.  Water beading up everywhere but right there.  No paint damage, though. Good luck with it.  ||||reg||11
Z||000004||rogergarrison||03-28-2001||05:54 PM||||before you run out to buy parts. unhook the battery and charge it for a couple hours, then reconnect it and see what happens. Maybe that way your ecm will forget any false signals.||||reg||1
Z||000005||loafer87gt||03-28-2001||07:12 PM||||Nice car man! I have actually been using your car as my wallpaper for the past coupla years now!||||reg||1
Z||000006||voyagerspe||03-28-2001||09:26 PM||||ouch!!!!!!!!<BR>Lightning can destroy a car and it doesnt even have to hit it.  <BR>1st Disconnect your battery and have it tested.<BR>2nd replace all your fuses (even ones that look good)<BR>3rd pray<BR>4th pray<BR>5th do a visual inspection of ALL visible wiring<BR>6th reconnect battery<BR>7th pray <BR>8th see what happens, and start replacing things that dont work right. like all your gauges, computer, sensors, wireing harness.<P>I hope that you have very minimal damage lighning sucks.  We had a JD compact tractor that to a pulse from a lightning strike it seemed fine at first after running it a little while weird things started to happen <BR>after about a week or replacing electical items we ended up taking it to the dealer and they did a complete overhaul of the electical system and all componets.  <BR>I hope all you lost was the fuel pump.<P>good luck<BR>||||reg||11
Z||000007||Raydar||03-29-2001||12:19 AM||||Are you sure your fuel pump relay didn't just stick, the last time you drove the car? If that were the case, it could have run your battery down <I>and</I> possibly triggered your alarm. Some alarms trigger on a change in voltage or current. Just a thought. (Although I have had lightning set off my alarms, too.)<BR>BTW... I actually had a bad alternator (leaky diode) cause my alarm to go off. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
